        <body>
            <div xml:id="d549">

                <pb facs="0555" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg521"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received Apr. 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 672.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reference to the Department’s
                    No. 647, of the 18th ultimo, relative to the threatened destruction by Cuban
                    insurgents of the property of the Ponupo Mining and Transportation Company, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith a copy, with translation, of a note from the
                    Spanish minister of state in reply to mine asking for protection to the property
                    of said company.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d549-a1.xml" xpointer="d549-a1"/>
